# Installing Secondary Artifacts

Sometimes you must install secondary artifacts after the main artifact. The main artifact must already be in the local repository.

To install a secondary artifact, use the `classifier` parameter.

Suppose that you want to install the sources for an old artifact, for example commons-logging-1.0.3. The [central repository](http://repo1.maven.org/maven2/commons-logging/commons-logging/1.0.3/) has only the main artifact and a `-javadoc` artifact for that version.

Package the sources into a JAR file on your local disk. Then run the following command:

```unknown
mvn ${project.groupId}:${project.artifactId}:${project.version}:install-file  -Dfile=path-to-commons-logging-sources.jar \
                                                                              -DgroupId=commons-logging \
                                                                              -DartifactId=commons-logging \ 
                                                                              -Dversion=1.0.3 \
                                                                              -Dpackaging=jar \
                                                                              -Dclassifier=sources
```

**Note**: Use the fully qualified path of a goal. This ensures that you use the preferred version of the maven-install-plugin. When you use `mvn install:install-file`, the plugin version depends on the POM or the Apache Maven version.
